  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n**Description:**  \nWhen a user cancels a withdrawal request (via the `cancelWithdrawal` function), the associated HYPE value (i.e., `totalHypeValueReturned`) is recorded in `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount`. Subsequently, an account with `MANAGER_ROLE` privileges can call the `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE` function, which reads the value of `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount`, resets it to zero, and re-delegates this HYPE amount through the `_distributeStake` function with the operation type `OperationType.SpotDeposit`.\n\nIn the `_distributeStake` function, when handling `SpotDeposit` or `RebalanceDeposit` types, the function calls `_convertTo8Decimals(amount, false)` to convert the 18-decimal `amount` into an 8-decimal `truncatedAmount`. The conversion logic is `truncatedAmount = amount / 1e10`, with the `roundUp` parameter set to `false`, meaning it always rounds down. However, unlike the handling of `UserDeposit` (see L464), the conversion process for `SpotDeposit` and `RebalanceDeposit` does not properly account for the remainder from `amount % 1e10`, i.e., the portion lost due to precision truncation. This remainder (less than `1e10` wei HYPE, equivalent to less than `1e-8` HYPE) is neither added back to `hypeBuffer` nor included in the `truncatedAmount` sent to L1.\n\n**Impact:**  \nEach time `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE` is used to re-delegate canceled withdrawal amounts, the rounding down in `_convertTo8Decimals`—without handling the remainder—causes `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount % 1e10` HYPE to be lost from the re-delegation process. This HYPE does not actually disappear from the system; it remains within the `StakingManager` contract (possibly in the contract’s ETH balance or an L1 account, depending on the fund flow implementation). However, it falls outside the protocol’s normal accounting and management mechanisms: it is neither recorded in `totalStaked`, explicitly tracked in `hypeBuffer`, nor delegated to validators to generate rewards.\n\nAs cancel-and-redelegate operations accumulate, this “lost” HYPE grows, becoming permanently stranded in the `StakingManager` contract, unusable by the protocol or returnable to users. This reduces the protocol’s capital efficiency and directly diminishes the potential profits for all kHYPE holders, effectively locking value permanently. Given that this issue could render protocol funds unproductive, it poses a high risk.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n1. Assume `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount` accumulates to `123.456789123456789123` HYPE (i.e., `123456789123456789123` wei).  \n2. `MANAGER_ROLE` calls `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE()`.  \n3. `_distributeStake(123456789123456789123, OperationType.SpotDeposit)` is triggered.  \n4. `_convertTo8Decimals(123456789123456789123, false)` performs the conversion.  \n5. The result is `truncatedAmount = 123456789123456789123 / 1e10 = 12345678912` (8 decimals).  \n6. The remainder is `remainder = 123456789123456789123 % 1e10 = 3456789123` wei.  \n7. `l1Write.sendCDeposit` is called with the parameter `12345678912`.  \n8. `_queueL1Operation` is called with the `amount` parameter as `12345678912`.  \n9. **Issue:** The remainder (`3456789123` wei HYPE) is unhandled—it is neither added back to `hypeBuffer` nor included in the L1 operation.  \n10. This HYPE value is permanently lost from the delegation cycle and stranded in the `StakingManager` contract.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nIt is recommended to modify the `_distributeStake` function to handle remainders from `_convertTo8Decimals` for `SpotDeposit` and `RebalanceDeposit` types, aligning their behavior with `UserDeposit` by adding the remainder back to `hypeBuffer`. The specific changes are as follows:\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/StakingManager.sol\n+++ b/src/StakingManager.sol\n@@ -484,15 +484,25 @@\n  \n              // 3. Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n              _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, operationType);\n-         } else if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit) {\n+         } else if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit || operationType == OperationType.RebalanceDeposit) { // Combine SpotDeposit and RebalanceDeposit logic\n              // For SpotDeposit, transfer the amount from spot balance to staking balance first\n              uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n-             require(truncatedAmount <= type(uint64).max, \"Amount exceeds uint64 max\");\n+             // require(truncatedAmount <= type(uint64).max, \"Amount exceeds uint64 max\"); // Check already included in _convertTo8Decimals\n+ \n+             // Handle remainder for SpotDeposit and RebalanceDeposit, aligning with UserDeposit\n+             uint256 remainder = amount % 1e10;\n+             if (remainder > 0) {\n+                 // Add remainder back to hypeBuffer\n+                 hypeBuffer += remainder;\n+                 // No need to subtract remainder from amount, as truncatedAmount already uses the floored value\n+                 emit BufferIncreased(remainder, hypeBuffer); // Emit buffer change event\n+             }\n  \n              // 1. Use cDeposit to transfer the amount from spot balance to staking balance\n-             l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n+             // Only send cDeposit if truncatedAmount > 0 to avoid unnecessary L1 calls\n+             if (truncatedAmount > 0) {\n+                 l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n+             }\n  \n              // 2. Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n-             _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, OperationType.RebalanceDeposit);\n-         } else if (operationType == OperationType.RebalanceDeposit) {\n-             // For RebalanceDeposit, only queue the operation\n-             uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n- \n-             // Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n              _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, operationType); // Use original operationType\n          } else {\n              revert(\"unrecognized operation type\");\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Result\n```bash\n[PASS] testPrecisionLoss() (gas: 254296)\nLogs:\n  = Testing Vulnerable StakingManager =\n  Original amount: 1000000005000000000\n  Original amount (wei): 1000000005000000000\n  Remainder (wei): 5000000000\n  Truncated amount (8 decimals): 100000000\n  Truncated amount (wei): 1000000000000000000\n  Recorded cancelled amount: 1000000005000000000\n  \nAfter redelegation:\n  Amount sent to L1 (8 decimals): 100000000\n  Amount sent to L1 (wei): 1000000000000000000\n  Expected precision loss (wei): 5000000000\n  Actual precision loss (wei): 5000000000\n  Value trapped in contract (wei): 5000000000\n  Buffer amount (wei): 0\n  \n= Testing Fixed StakingManager =\n  Original amount: 1000000005000000000\n  Original amount (wei): 1000000005000000000\n  Remainder (wei): 5000000000\n  Truncated amount (8 decimals): 100000000\n  Truncated amount (wei): 1000000000000000000\n  Recorded cancelled amount: 1000000005000000000\n  \nAfter redelegation:\n  Amount sent to L1 (8 decimals): 100000000\n  Amount sent to L1 (wei): 1000000000000000000\n  Expected precision loss (wei): 5000000000\n  Actual precision loss (wei): 5000000000\n  Value trapped in contract (wei): 0\n  Buffer amount (wei): 5000000000\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 858.46µs (257.83µs CPU time)\n\nRan 2 tests for test/Counter.t.sol:CounterTest\n[PASS] testFuzz_SetNumber(uint256) (runs: 256, μ: 30888, ~: 31277)\n[PASS] test_Increment() (gas: 31293)\nSuite result: ok. 2 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 3.68ms (3.26ms CPU time)\n```\n\n## POC\n```solidity\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\n\ncontract PrecisionLossPOC is Test {\n    MockL1Write public l1Write;\n    MockValidatorManager public validatorManager;\n    VulnerableStakingManager public vulnerableStakingManager;\n    FixedStakingManager public fixedStakingManager;\n    address constant VALIDATOR = address(0x42);\n    address constant USER = address(0x100);\n    address constant MANAGER = address(0x200);\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        l1Write = new MockL1Write();\n        validatorManager = new MockValidatorManager();\n        validatorManager.setValidator(VALIDATOR);\n        vulnerableStakingManager = new VulnerableStakingManager(\n            address(l1Write),\n            address(validatorManager)\n        );\n        fixedStakingManager = new FixedStakingManager(\n            address(l1Write),\n            address(validatorManager)\n        );\n        vulnerableStakingManager.grantRole(vulnerableStakingManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), MANAGER);\n        fixedStakingManager.grantRole(fixedStakingManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), MANAGER);\n        vm.deal(address(vulnerableStakingManager), 100 ether);\n        vm.deal(address(fixedStakingManager), 100 ether);\n    }\n    \n    function testPrecisionLoss() public {\n        uint256 amount = 1 ether + 5 * 1e9;\n        console.log(\"= Testing Vulnerable StakingManager =\");\n        runTest(vulnerableStakingManager, amount, true);\n        console.log(\"\\n= Testing Fixed StakingManager =\");\n        runTest(fixedStakingManager, amount, false);\n    }\n    \n    function runTest(IStakingManager stakingManager, uint256 amount, bool isVulnerable) internal {\n        l1Write.reset();\n        uint256 remainder = amount % 1e10;\n        uint256 truncatedAmount8Decimals = amount / 1e10;\n        uint256 truncatedAmountWei = truncatedAmount8Decimals * 1e10;\n        vm.prank(MANAGER);\n        stakingManager.simulateCancelWithdrawal(amount);\n        console.log(\"Original amount:\", amount);\n        console.log(\"Original amount (wei):\", amount);\n        console.log(\"Remainder (wei):\", remainder);\n        console.log(\"Truncated amount (8 decimals):\", truncatedAmount8Decimals);\n        console.log(\"Truncated amount (wei):\", truncatedAmountWei);\n        uint256 cancelledAmount = stakingManager.cancelledWithdrawalAmount();\n        console.log(\"Recorded cancelled amount:\", cancelledAmount);\n        vm.prank(MANAGER);\n        stakingManager.redelegateWithdrawnHYPE();\n        uint256 sentToL1 = l1Write.totalSentToL1();\n        uint256 sentToL1InWei = sentToL1 * 1e10;\n        console.log(\"\\nAfter redelegation:\");\n        console.log(\"Amount sent to L1 (8 decimals):\", sentToL1);\n        console.log(\"Amount sent to L1 (wei):\", sentToL1InWei);\n        uint256 expectedLoss = remainder;\n        uint256 actualLoss = amount - sentToL1InWei;\n        console.log(\"Expected precision loss (wei):\", expectedLoss);\n        console.log(\"Actual precision loss (wei):\", actualLoss);\n        uint256 trappedValue = stakingManager.trappedValue();\n        uint256 bufferValue = stakingManager.hypeBuffer();\n        console.log(\"Value trapped in contract (wei):\", trappedValue);\n        console.log(\"Buffer amount (wei):\", bufferValue);\n        if (isVulnerable) {\n            assertEq(actualLoss, expectedLoss, \"Actual loss should match expected loss\");\n            assertEq(trappedValue, expectedLoss, \"Trapped value should equal expected loss\");\n            assertEq(bufferValue, 0, \"Vulnerable version should not use buffer\");\n        } else {\n            assertEq(bufferValue, expectedLoss, \"Buffer should contain precision loss\");\n            assertEq(trappedValue, 0, \"Fixed contract should have no trapped value\");\n            assertEq(actualLoss, expectedLoss, \"Actual loss should match what's in buffer\");\n            assertEq(sentToL1InWei + bufferValue, amount, \"Total value should be preserved\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ninterface IStakingManager {\n    function MANAGER_ROLE() external view returns (bytes32);\n    function grantRole(bytes32 role, address account) external;\n    function simulateCancelWithdrawal(uint256 amount) external;\n    function redelegateWithdrawnHYPE() external;\n    function cancelledWithdrawalAmount() external view returns (uint256);\n    function totalRedelegated() external view returns (uint256);\n    function trappedValue() external view returns (uint256);\n    function hypeBuffer() external view returns (uint256);\n}\n\ncontract MockL1Write {\n    uint256 public totalSentToL1;\n    struct Operation {\n        uint64 amount;\n        bytes4 operationType;\n    }\n    Operation[] public operations;\n    \n    function sendCDeposit(uint64 amount) external {\n        operations.push(Operation(amount, bytes4(keccak256(\"cDeposit\"))));\n        totalSentToL1 += amount;\n    }\n    \n    function getOperationsCount() external view returns (uint256) {\n        return operations.length;\n    }\n    \n    function reset() external {\n        delete operations;\n        totalSentToL1 = 0;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockValidatorManager {\n    address public validator;\n    \n    function setValidator(address _validator) external {\n        validator = _validator;\n    }\n    \n    function getDelegation(address) external view returns (address) {\n        return validator;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract VulnerableStakingManager is IStakingManager {\n    bytes32 public constant MANAGER_ROLE = keccak256(\"MANAGER_ROLE\");\n    enum OperationType {\n        UserDeposit,\n        SpotDeposit,\n        RebalanceDeposit,\n        UserWithdrawal,\n        RebalanceWithdrawal\n    }\n    MockL1Write public l1Write;\n    MockValidatorManager public validatorManager;\n    uint256 private _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n    uint256 public hypeBuffer;\n    uint256 public totalRedelegatedAmount;\n    mapping(bytes32 => mapping(address => bool)) private _roles;\n    \n    constructor(address _l1Write, address _validatorManager) {\n        l1Write = MockL1Write(_l1Write);\n        validatorManager = MockValidatorManager(_validatorManager);\n        _roles[MANAGER_ROLE][msg.sender] = true;\n    }\n    \n    function grantRole(bytes32 role, address account) public override {\n        _roles[role][account] = true;\n    }\n    \n    modifier onlyRole(bytes32 role) {\n        require(_roles[role][msg.sender], \"Caller doesn't have role\");\n        _;\n    }\n    \n    function cancelledWithdrawalAmount() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        return _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n    }\n    \n    function totalRedelegated() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        return totalRedelegatedAmount;\n    }\n    \n    function trappedValue() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        if (_cancelledWithdrawalAmount == 0 && totalRedelegatedAmount > 0) {\n            uint256 sentToL1InWei = l1Write.totalSentToL1() * 1e10;\n            if (totalRedelegatedAmount > sentToL1InWei) {\n                return totalRedelegatedAmount - sentToL1InWei;\n            }\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    function simulateCancelWithdrawal(uint256 amount) external override onlyRole(MANAGER_ROLE) {\n        _cancelledWithdrawalAmount += amount;\n    }\n    \n    function redelegateWithdrawnHYPE() external override onlyRole(MANAGER_ROLE) {\n        require(_cancelledWithdrawalAmount > 0, \"No cancelled withdrawals\");\n        uint256 amount = _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n        _cancelledWithdrawalAmount = 0;\n        totalRedelegatedAmount += amount;\n        _distributeStake(amount, OperationType.SpotDeposit);\n    }\n    \n    function _distributeStake(uint256 amount, OperationType operationType) internal {\n        address validator = validatorManager.getDelegation(address(this));\n        if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit) {\n            uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n            l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    function _convertTo8Decimals(uint256 amount, bool roundUp) internal pure returns (uint256 truncatedAmount) {\n        truncatedAmount = amount / 1e10;\n        if (roundUp && amount % 1e10 > 0) {\n            truncatedAmount += 1;\n        }\n        return truncatedAmount;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract FixedStakingManager is IStakingManager {\n    bytes32 public constant MANAGER_ROLE = keccak256(\"MANAGER_ROLE\");\n    enum OperationType {\n        UserDeposit,\n        SpotDeposit,\n        RebalanceDeposit,\n        UserWithdrawal,\n        RebalanceWithdrawal\n    }\n    MockL1Write public l1Write;\n    MockValidatorManager public validatorManager;\n    uint256 private _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n    uint256 public hypeBuffer;\n    uint256 public totalRedelegatedAmount;\n    mapping(bytes32 => mapping(address => bool)) private _roles;\n    event BufferIncreased(uint256 amountAdded, uint256 newTotal);\n    \n    constructor(address _l1Write, address _validatorManager) {\n        l1Write = MockL1Write(_l1Write);\n        validatorManager = MockValidatorManager(_validatorManager);\n        _roles[MANAGER_ROLE][msg.sender] = true;\n    }\n    \n    function grantRole(bytes32 role, address account) public override {\n        _roles[role][account] = true;\n    }\n    \n    modifier onlyRole(bytes32 role) {\n        require(_roles[role][msg.sender], \"Caller doesn't have role\");\n        _;\n    }\n    \n    function cancelledWithdrawalAmount() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        return _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n    }\n    \n    function totalRedelegated() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        return totalRedelegatedAmount;\n    }\n    \n    function trappedValue() external view override returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    function simulateCancelWithdrawal(uint256 amount) external override onlyRole(MANAGER_ROLE) {\n        _cancelledWithdrawalAmount += amount;\n    }\n    \n    function redelegateWithdrawnHYPE() external override onlyRole(MANAGER_ROLE) {\n        require(_cancelledWithdrawalAmount > 0, \"No cancelled withdrawals\");\n        uint256 amount = _cancelledWithdrawalAmount;\n        _cancelledWithdrawalAmount = 0;\n        totalRedelegatedAmount += amount;\n        _distributeStake(amount, OperationType.SpotDeposit);\n    }\n    \n    function _distributeStake(uint256 amount, OperationType operationType) internal {\n        address validator = validatorManager.getDelegation(address(this));\n        if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit) {\n            uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n            uint256 remainder = amount % 1e10;\n            if (remainder > 0) {\n                hypeBuffer += remainder;\n                emit BufferIncreased(remainder, hypeBuffer);\n            }\n            if (truncatedAmount > 0) {\n                l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    function _convertTo8Decimals(uint256 amount, bool roundUp) internal pure returns (uint256 truncatedAmount) {\n        truncatedAmount = amount / 1e10;\n        if (roundUp && amount % 1e10 > 0) {\n            truncatedAmount += 1;\n        }\n        return truncatedAmount;\n    }\n}\n\n```",
