ate rewards.\n\nAs cancel-and-redelegate operations accumulate, this “lost” HYPE grows, becoming permanently stranded in the `StakingManager` contract, unusable by the protocol or returnable to users. This reduces the protocol’s capital efficiency and directly diminishes the potential profits for all kHYPE holders, effectively locking value permanently. Given that this issue could render protocol funds unproductive, it poses a high risk.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n1. Assume `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount` accumulates to `123.456789123456789123` HYPE (i.e., `123456789123456789123` wei).  \n2. `MANAGER_ROLE` calls `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE()`.  \n3. `_distributeStake(123456789123456789123, OperationType.SpotDeposit)` is triggered.  \n4. `_convertTo8Decimals(123456789123456789123, false)` performs the conversion.  \n5. The result is `truncatedAmount = 123456789123456789123 / 1e10 = 12345678912` (8 decimals).  \n6. The remainder is `remainder = 123456789123456789123 % 1e10 = 3456789123` wei.  \n7. `l1Write.sendCDeposit` is called with the parameter `12345678912`.  \n8. `_queueL1Operation` is called with the `amount` parameter as `12345678912`.  \n9. **Issue:** The remainder (`3456789123` wei HYPE) is unhandled—it is neither added back to `hypeBuffer` nor included in the L1 operation.  \n10. This HYPE value is permanently lost from the delegation cycle and stranded in the `StakingManager` contract.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nIt is recommended to modify the `_distributeStake` function to handle remainders from `_convertTo8Decimals` for `SpotDeposit` and `RebalanceDeposit` types, aligning their behavior with `UserDeposit` by adding the remainder back to `hypeBuffer`. The specific changes are as follows:\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/StakingManager.sol\n+++ b/src/StakingManager.sol\n@@ -484,15 +484,25 @@\n  \n              // 3. Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n              _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, operationType);\n-         } else if (operationT