      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n**Description:**  \nWhen a user cancels a withdrawal request (via the `cancelWithdrawal` function), the associated HYPE value (i.e., `totalHypeValueReturned`) is recorded in `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount`. Subsequently, an account with `MANAGER_ROLE` privileges can call the `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE` function, which reads the value of `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount`, resets it to zero, and re-delegates this HYPE amount through the `_distributeStake` function with the operation type `OperationType.SpotDeposit`.\n\nIn the `_distributeStake` function, when handling `SpotDeposit` or `RebalanceDeposit` types, the function calls `_convertTo8Decimals(amount, false)` to convert the 18-decimal `amount` into an 8-decimal `truncatedAmount`. The conversion logic is `truncatedAmount = amount / 1e10`, with the `roundUp` parameter set to `false`, meaning it always rounds down. However, unlike the handling of `UserDeposit` (see L464), the conversion process for `SpotDeposit` and `RebalanceDeposit` does not properly account for the remainder from `amount % 1e10`, i.e., the portion lost due to precision truncation. This remainder (less than `1e10` wei HYPE, equivalent to less than `1e-8` HYPE) is neither added back to `hypeBuffer` nor included in the `truncatedAmount` sent to L1.\n\n**Impact:**  \nEach time `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE` is used to re-delegate canceled withdrawal amounts, the rounding down in `_convertTo8Decimals`—without handling the remainder—causes `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount % 1e10` HYPE to be lost from the re-delegation process. This HYPE does not actually disappear from the system; it remains within the `StakingManager` contract (possibly in the contract’s ETH balance or an L1 account, depending on the fund flow implementation). However, it falls outside the protocol’s normal accounting and management mechanisms: it is neither recorded in `totalStaked`, explicitly tracked in `hypeBuffer`, nor delegated to validators to generate rewards.\n\nAs cancel-and-redelegate operations accumulate, this “lost” HYPE grows, becoming permanently stranded in the `StakingManager` contract, unusable by the protocol or returnable to users. This reduces the protocol’s capital efficiency and directly diminishes the potential profits for all kHYPE holders, effectively locking value permanently. Given that this issue could render protocol funds unproductive, it poses a high risk.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n1. Assume `_cancelledWithdrawalAmount` accumulates to `123.456789123456789123` HYPE (i.e., `123456789123456789123` wei).  \n2. `MANAGER_ROLE` calls `redelegateWithdrawnHYPE()`.  \n3. `_distributeStake(123456789123456789123, OperationType.SpotDeposit)` is triggered.  \n4. `_convertTo8Decimals(123456789123456789123, false)` performs the conversion.  \n5. The result is `truncatedAmount = 123456789123456789123 / 1e10 = 12345678912` (8 decimals).  \n6. The remainder is `remainder = 123456789123456789123 % 1e10 = 3456789123` wei.  \n7. `l1Write.sendCDeposit` is called with the parameter `12345678912`.  \n8. `_queueL1Operation` is called with the `amount` parameter as `12345678912`.  \n9. **Issue:** The remainder (`3456789123` wei HYPE) is unhandled—it is neither added back to `hypeBuffer` nor included in the L1 operation.  \n10. This HYPE value is permanently lost from the delegation cycle and stranded in the `StakingManager` contract.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nIt is recommended to modify the `_distributeStake` function to handle remainders from `_convertTo8Decimals` for `SpotDeposit` and `RebalanceDeposit` types, aligning their behavior with `UserDeposit` by adding the remainder back to `hypeBuffer`. The specific changes are as follows:\n\n```diff\n--- a/src/StakingManager.sol\n+++ b/src/StakingManager.sol\n@@ -484,15 +484,25 @@\n  \n              // 3. Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n              _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, operationType);\n-         } else if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit) {\n+         } else if (operationType == OperationType.SpotDeposit || operationType == OperationType.RebalanceDeposit) { // Combine SpotDeposit and RebalanceDeposit logic\n              // For SpotDeposit, transfer the amount from spot balance to staking balance first\n              uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n-             require(truncatedAmount <= type(uint64).max, \"Amount exceeds uint64 max\");\n+             // require(truncatedAmount <= type(uint64).max, \"Amount exceeds uint64 max\"); // Check already included in _convertTo8Decimals\n+ \n+             // Handle remainder for SpotDeposit and RebalanceDeposit, aligning with UserDeposit\n+             uint256 remainder = amount % 1e10;\n+             if (remainder > 0) {\n+                 // Add remainder back to hypeBuffer\n+                 hypeBuffer += remainder;\n+                 // No need to subtract remainder from amount, as truncatedAmount already uses the floored value\n+                 emit BufferIncreased(remainder, hypeBuffer); // Emit buffer change event\n+             }\n  \n              // 1. Use cDeposit to transfer the amount from spot balance to staking balance\n-             l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n+             // Only send cDeposit if truncatedAmount > 0 to avoid unnecessary L1 calls\n+             if (truncatedAmount > 0) {\n+                 l1Write.sendCDeposit(uint64(truncatedAmount));\n+             }\n  \n              // 2. Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n-             _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, OperationType.RebalanceDeposit);\n-         } else if (operationType == OperationType.RebalanceDeposit) {\n-             // For RebalanceDeposit, only queue the operation\n-             uint256 truncatedAmount = _convertTo8Decimals(amount, false);\n- \n-             // Queue the delegation operation (8 decimals)\n              _queueL1Operation(validator, truncatedAmount, operationType); // Use original operationType\n          } else {\n              revert(\"unrecognized operation type\");\n```",
